\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Shell model with two valence particles. The core orbits are fully occupied (inert core with energy $E_C$; red: protons, blue: neutrons), the two valence particles (here neutrons) occupy orbits $j_1$, $j_2$ of the valence space and interact via the residual interaction $V(1,2)$; the orbits above the valence space are excluded.}}{22}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:valspace}{{8}{22}{Shell model with two valence particles. The core orbits are fully occupied (inert core with energy $E_C$; red: protons, blue: neutrons), the two valence particles (here neutrons) occupy orbits $j_1$, $j_2$ of the valence space and interact via the residual interaction $V(1,2)$; the orbits above the valence space are excluded}{figure.8}{}}
